FILE-14: keep the remaining length right after a quoted token

gettokens() keeps len, the number of characters left on the line. For a
token that starts with a quote, it subtracted the length up to the first
separator, but then moved past the whole quoted token and its closing
quote. The two disagreed: without spaces in the quotes len ended one too
short, so the last token on the line kept its newline; with spaces it
ended too long, so the scan ran past the end of the line. len is now
recomputed from the position of the closing quote.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply FILE-14_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/input2.c b/src/input2.c
index 220c757..b9876e0 100644
--- a/src/input2.c
+++ b/src/input2.c
@@ -608,6 +608,7 @@ int  gettokens(char *s, char** Tok, int maxToks, char *comment)
             {
                 s++;                           // Start token after quote
                 m = (int)strcspn(s,"\"\n\r");  // Find end quote (or EOL)
+                len = (int)strlen(s + m) - 1;  // Length after end quote
             }
             s[m] = '\0';                 // Null-terminate the token
             Tok[n] = s;                  // Save pointer to token
